{"name":"Hotspot","hex":"#ff4433","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hotspot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of hot spot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hotspot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hotspot (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, hotspots are volcanic locales thought to be fed by underlying mantle that is anomalously hot compared with the surrounding mantle. Examples include the Hawaii, Iceland, and Yellowstone hotspots. A hotspot's position on the Earth's surface is independent of tectonic plate boundaries, and so hotspots may create a chain of volcanoes as the plates move above them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Hawaii_hotspot_cross-sectional_diagram.jpg/330px-Hawaii_hotspot_cross-sectional_diagram.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotspot_(geology)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Hawaii_hotspot.jpg/500px-Hawaii_hotspot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Hawaii_hotspot.jpg/1280px-Hawaii_hotspot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Hawaii_hotspot.jpg/500px-Hawaii_hotspot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Over millions of years, the Pacific plate has moved over the Hawaii hotspot, creating a trail of underwater mountains that stretches across the Pacific.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHawaii_hotspot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Puu_Oo_cropped.jpg/500px-Puu_Oo_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Puu_Oo_cropped.jpg/500px-Puu_Oo_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kilauea is the most active shield volcano in the world. The volcano erupted from 1983 to 2018 and is part of the Hawaiian–Emperor seamount chain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuu_Oo_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mauna_Loa_Volcano.jpg/500px-Mauna_Loa_Volcano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mauna_Loa_Volcano.jpg/500px-Mauna_Loa_Volcano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mauna Loa is a large shield volcano. Its last eruption was in 2022 and it is part of the Hawaiian–Emperor seamount chain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMauna_Loa_Volcano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Bowie_Seamount1.jpg/500px-Bowie_Seamount1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Bowie_Seamount1.jpg/500px-Bowie_Seamount1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bowie Seamount is a dormant submarine volcano and part of the Kodiak-Bowie Seamount chain.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABowie_Seamount1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg/500px-Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg/1280px-Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg/500px-Axial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Axial Seamount is the youngest seamount of the Cobb–Eickelberg Seamount chain. Its last eruption was in 2015.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAxial_Exaggerated_Bathymetry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg/500px-Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg/1280px-Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg/500px-Mauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mauna Kea is the tallest volcano in the Hawaiian–Emperor seamount chain. Many cinder cones have been emplaced around its summit.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMauna_Kea_from_the_ocean.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Hual%C4%81lai_1996.jpg/500px-Hual%C4%81lai_1996.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Hual%C4%81lai_1996.jpg/500px-Hual%C4%81lai_1996.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hualalai is a massive shield volcano in the Hawaiian–Emperor seamount chain. Its last eruption was in 1801.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHual%C4%81lai_1996.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CourtHotspots.png/500px-CourtHotspots.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CourtHotspots.png/500px-CourtHotspots.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","a